The key bound is that active display requires `v_cnt < 100`. One clock later, `v_cnt` is at most 100—still before the vertical-sync pulse at counts 104–107. The lemmas separate that bound from the sync transition. The temporal operators refer to successive clock samples. ([fpga.mit.edu](https://fpga.mit.edu/6205/_static/F25/documentation/1800-2017.pdf))

<json>
{
  "lemmas": [
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_1; @(posedge clk) s_nexttime (disp_ena |-> (v_cnt < v_pixels)); endproperty",
      "explanation": "After every clock edge, disp_ena is either cleared by reset or computed from the updated counters. Thus an asserted disp_ena implies v_cnt is in the active-pixel range. The initial nexttime avoids relying on unconstrained initial register values."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_2; @(posedge clk) (v_cnt < v_pixels) |=> (v_cnt < (v_pixels + v_fp)); endproperty",
      "explanation": "The vertical counter holds, increments by at most one, or resets to zero. From below 100, it therefore remains below the sync-pulse start at 104 on the next sample."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_3; @(posedge clk) s_nexttime ((v_cnt < (v_pixels + v_fp)) |-> (v_sync != $past(v_sync))); endproperty",
      "explanation": "Whenever the newly sampled vertical count is before the pulse, the preceding edge toggled v_sync; reset also toggles it. Together with the first two lemmas, this gives the toggle required by prop."
    }
  ]
}
</json>

