Concurrent assertions sample values before the clocked updates, and `s_nexttime` evaluates at the next clock sample. The first lemma therefore starts one sample later, when `disp_ena` has been computed from the counters—even if their initial values were unconstrained. ([fpga.mit.edu](https://fpga.mit.edu/6205/_static/F25/documentation/1800-2017.pdf))

